From: HD Satelit <contact@hdsatelit.com>
Subject: [PATCH] h265 writer: TS input without the extra zero byte, PES with DTS

On HiSilicon (Viper 4K V20, 3798MV200) the DVB layer rejected every HEVC packet written from a TS source
("pes start byte = 0 0 0" in the kernel log, the HEVC decoder opened but got no frame), while H.264 played.
The H.264 writer puts the Annex B data right after the PES header, with the DTS; do the same for H.265.

--- a/output/writer/mipsel/h265.c
+++ b/output/writer/mipsel/h265.c
@@ -239,14 +239,13 @@
             PacketLength     += call->private_size;
         }
 
-        iov[ic].iov_base = "";
-        iov[ic++].iov_len = 1;
-
+        /* no extra zero byte between the PES header and the Annex B data, and the DTS as for H.264: the HiSilicon
+           DVB layer rejected every packet ("pes start byte = 0 0 0") and the HEVC decoder got no frame */
         iov[ic].iov_base  = call->data;
         iov[ic++].iov_len = call->len;
         PacketLength     += call->len;
 
-        iov[0].iov_len = InsertPesHeader(PesHeader, -1, MPEG_VIDEO_PES_START_CODE, VideoPts, FakeStartCode);
+        iov[0].iov_len = InsertPesHeaderWithDts(PesHeader, -1, MPEG_VIDEO_PES_START_CODE, VideoPts, call->Dts, FakeStartCode);
 
         return call->WriteV(call->fd, iov, ic);
     }
